ALTCPM and ZXCPM related tools
________
The kits require a command line CP/M emulator.

________
BASCOM-ALTCPM-XDEV.ZIP works also in ZXBASIC mode but needs the z88dk/support/rel/rebase.c program.

________
The BDS C kit is a beefed setup built around the original ALTCPM base libraries and compiler
(Beware it is previous to version 1.5, the later versions are slightly different).
It should, at some extent, permit to build historical programs which hardly could be built natively
on an ALTCPM system. Also the library is slightly extended, still trying to keep it compatible 
with CP/M 1.4

biosh.asm and cfsize.asm are backports of BDS C functions borrowed from later compiler versions.
l2.c is the source code of a manipulated ALTCPM version of the Mark of the Unicorn linker,
it is much more verbose than the original one, today it is easier to keep the console output history !
Usually you won't need those extra files, they are already present in built form in ALTCPM-BDSC-XDEV-v3.ZIP

The refreshed DIO.H & DIO.CRL files, in turn, are optional but highly recommended in case of odd console output behaviors.
Many files in the "programs" section were built with this hacked variant.
Remember that, if used, dio.crl must stay on top (you should specify dio.crl as the first library in the linker command line).

